Package: fcitx5-slm-ime
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fcitx5, slm-ime-model (>= ${source:Version})
Recommends: xdg-utils
Breaks: slm-ime-server (<< 2.0.0)
Description: Japanese input method for fcitx5 using a small language model
 Input method engine of fcitx5. It turns typed romaji into hiragana and
 converts the reading to kanji-kana text with a small Transformer model that
 also reads the text before the cursor, computed on the CPU inside the engine.
 The alternative candidates of a bunsetsu come from Anthy, put in order by the
 model. Keys can be set by profile (Default, MS-IME, ATOK) or one by one.
 .
 The choices of the user are kept in ~/.local/share/slm-ime/user_history.tsv.
 After the installation, restart fcitx5 and add "SLM IME" to the input methods
 with fcitx5-configtool. Version 2 needs no conversion server: the
 slm-ime-server package of version 1 is removed.

Package: slm-ime-model
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Trained model of fcitx5-slm-ime
 Weights and tokenizer of the conversion model of fcitx5-slm-ime: a
 character-level Transformer encoder-decoder with about 60 million parameters,
 trained on pairs of a reading and kanji-kana text made from the Japanese
 Wikipedia and FineWeb-2 web pages.
